  "_about": "a greater flamingo standing: a compact oval body held level on very long pink legs -- bare tibia, the backward 'knee' (the ankle) half-way down, long tarsus, webbed feet -- the neck in its S, a small head and the thick bill bent down at its middle, pale pink with a black end; folded wings of crimson coverts, the black flight feathers showing along the rear edge under the drooping pink tertials (2026-11-08, review.py: bill root) The bill's root is faired into the face (horn `fair`): no hard collar where it leaves the skull. (2026-11-08, flamingo.py) ALOFT the folded tracts turn into the body and a spread wing of its own swings out feather by feather (nbwing.aloft): crimson coverts over the arm, black secondaries along its trailing edge, long black primaries on the hand -- no longer the folded wing itself swung out as loose blades. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/necks.py) The NECK is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along the chain of neck bones, not a tube a bone blended into the next: no bead at the joints. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/flynecks.py) ALOFT the neck is held nearly straight ahead with a slight sag: the neck sweep is skinned from the body along its bones with its hand-offs on the rest curve's bends (`knotsAt`, `spread`), and the neck bones' and head's `flyRot` set with them.",
